# CounselClear — minimal PRODUCTION environment.
#
# This is the small subset needed to run the PRODUCT in production (Render /
# Fly / a plain host). It deliberately omits the research/harness and
# upstream-utility variables in .env.example — none of those are part of the
# CounselClear product path. Copy to your platform's secret store; do NOT
# commit a filled-in copy.

# --- Authentication (pick ONE) -----------------------------------------------
# Option A: shared operator password (single-tenant pilot default).
# Required unless OIDC (Option B) is fully configured. Use a long random value.
COUNSELCLEAR_LOCAL_PASSWORD=

# Option B: OIDC SSO. Setting ALL THREE disables local login. The allowlist is
# fail-closed: empty means nobody can complete a login.
# COUNSELCLEAR_OIDC_ISSUER=https://your-idp.example.com
# COUNSELCLEAR_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# COUNSELCLEAR_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# COUNSELCLEAR_OIDC_ALLOWED=alice@firm.example,bob@firm.example

# --- State -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Writable root for the SQLite DB, write-once document custody store, auth
# secrets, and the audit chain. On Render/Fly this is the mounted disk.
COUNSELCLEAR_DATA_ROOT=/data

# Optional: point at managed Postgres instead of the embedded SQLite file
# (recommended once you run more than one API replica). Object custody stays
# on the filesystem regardless.
# COUNSELCLEAR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host:5432/counselclear

# --- Serving behind a TLS-terminating proxy ----------------------------------
# "true" always marks the session cookie Secure (correct behind Render/Fly/
# nginx TLS). "auto" (default) follows the request scheme; use "false" only
# for loopback HTTP dev.
COUNSELCLEAR_COOKIE_SECURE=true

# Single-origin deploy (deploy/Dockerfile.render): the API serves the built
# UI from this directory on the same origin. The image sets this already;
# override only if you relocate the export.
COUNSELCLEAR_STATIC_DIR=/app/web_out

# --- Jobs --------------------------------------------------------------------
# In-process worker (no docker-in-docker on a PaaS container). For true per-job
# container isolation, run as a native host process in docker mode instead —
# see docs/COUNSELCLEAR_PRODUCTION.md.
COUNSELCLEAR_WORKER_MODE=subprocess

# --- Safety defaults (usually leave as-is) -----------------------------------
# Keep interactive API docs (/docs, /openapi.json) closed on public deploys.
COUNSELCLEAR_ENABLE_DOCS=
# Live ClamAV definitions directory (falls back to the image's build-time seed).
# COUNSELCLEAR_CLAMAV_DB_DIR=/clamav-defs
